### 2c. Named stub / residual classes (do not greenwash)

1. **Std crypto math** — product surface is **gate-only and/or unaudited**. Load-bearing residual pack: `bootstrap/STDLIB_CRYPTO_MATH.oot`.  
   - Still `process_exit(1)` on public entry bodies (examples): `ed25519_ops`, `dilithium_ops`, `groth16_ops`, `double_ratchet_ops`, `kyber`.  
   - Some `_ops` now carry **partial synthetic math without exit** (`falcon_ops`, `secp256k1_ops`, `plonk_ops`) — still **not audited**, not constant-time proven, **not production crypto**.  
   - Pair files (`_types`, `_engine`, `_stubs`) may look complete; bodies are not a ship claim.
2. **Top-level hash/crypto facades** — `hash/sha256.oo`, `hash/blake3.oo` landed as process_exit stubs; many other `hash/*` / top-level `crypto/*` still untracked partials.
3. **Net surface** — 5 granular migrations only; majority still legacy `&NetCap`; sealed per-op map residual (`CAPS_MATRIX`).
4. **Hardware** — `src/hw` / `src/sys/hw` remain stub-class with `&SysCap` (no mass cap add).
5. **Domain libs (auto/fin/aero/bio/…)** — many `*_stubs.oo` / process_exit / partial engines; 250-lib ambition is residual (PM R5).
6. **Scratch tests** — root/`src` `test_*.oo` quarantine candidates (BATCH K); not library API.
7. **Layout dualism** — top-level `crypto/`/`db/`/`hw` vs `src/ooda/*` ownership unresolved (needs layout decision before freeze).

